    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d882">

                <pb facs="0945" n="933" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg933"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">764.71/9–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative in Hungary</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-07T20:00:00+02:00">September 7,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 10—1:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>551. My No. 531, September 5, section II.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d882-f1"/>
                    Hungarian Ministry for Foreign Affairs has submitted note of [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">to?</hi>] ACC (Allied Control Commission) that
                    information has been received Rumanian Prime Minister’s<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d882-f2"/> office has published order pertaining to expulsion of
                    Hungarians from Rumania. In accordance with alleged order Rumanian Office for
                    Nationalities is advised to expel Hungarians under the pretext of “Fascistic
                    activity, spreading of false rumors, fostering of sedition, lack of cooperation
                    with Russians and sabotage”. Persons expelled are not allowed to sell properties
                    and can only take limited amount of movable possessions. Expulsion order can
                    only be given orally and written orders are forbidden. Order allegedly provides
                    for publication of complaints against chauvinistic activities of Hungarians and
                    purpose is said to be to influence plebiscite in question of Rumanian-Hungarian
                    border which peace conference is thought likely to hold. Hungarian ACC is asked
                    to request Rumanian ACC to demand satisfactory reply from Rumanian Government in
                    this matter which Hungarians feel endangers friendly relations between two
                    countries. Text of note by despatch.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d882-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Dept as No. 551, repeated to Bucharest as No. 23.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
